Z||000011||batboy||06-27-2000||10:11 PM||||I bought a pair of 1986 Trans Am hood louvers like these in this pic from the Pontiac dealership for about $45. If you can find them in the salvage yard, they'd be much cheaper. Lots of things would work. A small scoop reversed wouild be cool. Monkey, everything in the radiator area under the hood is already open to the elements. I doubt much rain would spray out the hood vents, but maybe somebody that has them already can vouch for that.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/hoodlwr.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 06-27-2000).]||||reg||1
